            <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Release-notes template (installer.md §4). Sparkle renders this inside its
     recessed box; these styles supply the type inside it: 12.5px semibold
     version + dimmed date, then ·-led 11.5/1.5 lines, last line dimmer folding
     in the previous patch. Duplicate per release as
     dist/updates/Thermal-<version>.html and fill in real, user-visible
     changes — never commit messages. -->
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
    body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 12px 14px;
        background: rgb(28, 28, 31);
        font: 11.5px/1.5 -apple-system, "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;
        color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.62);
    }
    h2 {
        font-size: 12.5px;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: #F2F2F4;
        margin: 0 0 6px;
    }
    h2 .date {
        font-weight: 400;
        color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
        margin-left: 6px;
    }
    ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    li::before { content: "· "; }
    .prev { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h2>Thermal 1.0 <span class="date">Aug 24, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
    <li>First release — live temperatures, history, fans, throttle log, and heat sources, from the menu bar.</li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>
